cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Stuntdouble or its 4-Layer Cognitive Brain in your research, mods, or autonomous agent benchmarks, please cite it as below."
title: "Stuntdouble: Competent combat hand-over for story-driven single-player games"
abstract: "An open-source architecture and reverse-engineering protocol that hands a single-player game's combat to a competent autonomous agent and gives control back afterwards. The game's own AI is the foundation; Stuntdouble's 4-layer brain (Orchestrator, Regressive A* GOAP, Compensated Utility AI, 16-Slot Context Steering) is a competence layer that overrides only the native AI's weak moments, or drives alone when the native AI is unreachable. Composable behavior flags, a seam contract with safety interlocks, and a deterministic arena with automatic gates provide the evidence."
